WEBVTT

01:30.230 --> 01:35.240
Alliance

01:30.590 --> 01:33.770
So, why have you gathered us all here?

01:33.770 --> 01:36.090
We've really got a lot 
on our plates right now.

01:36.090 --> 01:37.360
Can we just go?

01:37.360 --> 01:38.820
Please, wait!

01:38.820 --> 01:43.620
I brought you all here to ask 
for your help with a plan.

01:43.620 --> 01:45.250
A plan?

01:45.250 --> 01:49.870
Yes. If the eight of us work together, 
we can all share the prize,

01:49.870 --> 01:53.120
and escape the Liar Game 
while we're at it!

01:53.980 --> 01:55.150
No way!

01:55.150 --> 01:56.620
How?!

01:58.380 --> 02:01.470
I put my heart and soul into 
explaining things to them.

02:02.240 --> 02:03.600
And in the end...

02:04.630 --> 02:06.070
Wow!

02:06.070 --> 02:07.770
I like this plan!

02:07.770 --> 02:11.360
But we'd each only win 
a little over 40 million yen.

02:11.360 --> 02:13.850
Forty million is more than enough!

02:13.850 --> 02:16.400
Beats being 100 million 
in debt if we lose.

02:16.400 --> 02:19.090
I'd count myself lucky just to break even!

02:19.090 --> 02:21.270
Did you think all this up?

02:21.270 --> 02:24.530
No, it was him. Akiyama-san.

02:24.530 --> 02:26.910
Akiyama-san, you rock!

02:26.910 --> 02:27.790
Wait, huh?

02:27.790 --> 02:31.040
Michiko Takada

02:28.110 --> 02:30.720
His nametag says something different...

02:31.050 --> 02:34.540
He's participating on 
behalf of someone else.

02:35.800 --> 02:37.790
A ringer, eh?

02:37.790 --> 02:40.970
Still, can this really be so easy?

02:40.970 --> 02:43.690
What if the tournament office 
cheats or something?

02:43.690 --> 02:45.760
They won't cheat.

02:45.760 --> 02:47.550
They have no reason to.

02:47.550 --> 02:49.570
What do you mean?

02:49.570 --> 02:55.200
These games are designed for them to make 
big money without the need to cheat.

02:55.570 --> 02:57.840
In order to keep your full prize,

02:57.840 --> 03:00.100
you have to proceed to the next round.

03:00.700 --> 03:02.580
If you want to drop out,

03:02.580 --> 03:05.260
you have to return half of your winnings.

03:06.410 --> 03:11.330
There's a 50% house cut baked in.

03:11.330 --> 03:13.080
I see...

03:13.620 --> 03:17.980
But how can we be sure none 
of us will betray our alliance?

03:17.980 --> 03:19.090
What do you mean?

03:20.260 --> 03:26.530
This plan requires one winner 
to take the pot for the rest.

03:26.890 --> 03:33.390
Isn't it possible the winner might leave
 without sharing their winnings?

03:33.390 --> 03:34.720
Not a problem.

03:34.720 --> 03:37.230
If you agree to participate in this plan,

03:37.230 --> 03:39.830
we'll be hammering out
 an ironclad contract.

03:40.800 --> 03:44.370
I'm in. It's best to keep it all business.

03:44.370 --> 03:47.570
A contract would certainly 
establish trust.

03:48.640 --> 03:51.150
And so, we wrote up a contract.

03:52.120 --> 03:56.190
On this day, the 21st of June, 2026, I hereby swear to act as part of a team of eight 
in Minority Rule, the second round of the Liar Game, under the following conditions:

03:52.120 --> 03:59.880
1.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hAs part of the team, I will act as decided in advance by the team.

03:52.120 --> 03:59.880
2.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hThe winner of this second-round game, in order to drop out before the third,
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hwill pay half of the 2.1 billion prize money (1.05 billion yen) to the LGT Office.

03:52.120 --> 03:59.880
3.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hOf the remaining 1.05 billion yen, the winner will pay the 100-million-yen debt of each of the seven prior losers,
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\htotaling 700 million yen.

03:52.120 --> 03:59.880
4.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hThe remaining 350 million yen will be split among the eight team members in equal amounts of 43.75 million yen.

03:52.120 --> 03:55.380
It obligated all of us to vote 
in the assigned manner,

03:55.380 --> 03:59.880
and for the final winner to divide 
the prize as agreed in advance.

04:00.160 --> 04:04.720
Anyone failing to follow the rules 
would be forced to pay full damages.

04:02.880 --> 04:05.390
Nao Kanzaki

04:02.880 --> 04:05.390
Jun Hosoe

04:02.880 --> 04:05.390
Reina Nishihara

04:03.660 --> 04:05.390
Yuki Makihara

04:05.390 --> 04:09.470
This will get us through, won't it?

04:09.470 --> 04:12.840
But why did you choose the six of us?

04:13.220 --> 04:19.220
In truth, there's someone dangerous 
we're calling "X" among the participants.

04:19.220 --> 04:21.730
Someone dangerous? "X"?

04:22.610 --> 04:25.170
The player named Michiko Takada

04:25.170 --> 04:29.400
came here to return the 100 million 
she'd won in the first round.

04:30.040 --> 04:33.940
But a certain young man pretended 
to be a Liar Game official

04:33.940 --> 04:36.400
and stole her 100 million.

04:37.370 --> 04:43.670
I see. So you chose five women 
and my decidedly not-young self.

04:43.670 --> 04:48.920
And Akiyama-san is participating 
as Takada-san's proxy?

04:48.920 --> 04:54.050
Does X have any distinguishing features? 
Is there a player you suspect?

04:54.050 --> 04:56.300
We have no idea.

04:56.300 --> 04:58.150
I find myself suspecting everyone...

04:58.560 --> 05:01.010
Especially Number 15.

05:01.570 --> 05:03.810
Number 15?! What a coincidence!

05:04.080 --> 05:08.560
I also thought he was behaving strangely!

05:08.560 --> 05:10.250
You did, Hitomi-san?

05:10.250 --> 05:13.030
I mean, he acts like he doesn't 
have a care in the world!

05:13.330 --> 05:18.820
If he's got a 100-million-yen check
 in his pocket, that would explain it.

05:19.730 --> 05:22.630
I knew it! He's X!

05:23.680 --> 05:26.400
Enough of the cloak-and-dagger drama.

05:26.400 --> 05:30.520
As long as he's not on our team, 
our victory is guaranteed.

05:30.520 --> 05:32.800
For now, at least.

05:33.810 --> 05:36.750
This is such a huge relief, though.

05:36.750 --> 05:40.320
We have a foolproof strategy, 
so we can just rest easy now, right?

05:40.320 --> 05:42.650
We absolutely cannot rest easy!

05:42.650 --> 05:46.140
Most of all, we have to watch out for X!

05:46.140 --> 05:50.080
What if he catches wind of our plan
 and tries to sabotage us?

05:50.080 --> 05:54.080
Then I guess we should make sure 
no one knows about our group.

05:54.080 --> 05:55.380
That's right.

05:55.380 --> 05:59.470
When the game starts tomorrow, 
let's refrain from any team huddles.

05:59.470 --> 06:02.720
Instead, talk to the other players
 as much as possible.

06:02.720 --> 06:05.620
Though I'm not sure how much 
anyone will want to talk.

06:05.970 --> 06:07.950
We still have to try.

06:07.950 --> 06:10.480
Number 15, in particular, needs 
to be watched like a hawk.

06:10.790 --> 06:13.600
Let's make this plan a success!

06:13.600 --> 06:14.350
Right?

06:14.890 --> 06:15.980
Right!

06:21.650 --> 06:25.850
We will now begin the first 
round of Minority Rule.

06:25.850 --> 06:29.240
Our historic first questioner 
of the game will be...

06:30.010 --> 06:32.990
Number 1, please come up to the stage.

06:33.990 --> 06:37.750
B-Between baseball and soccer...

06:37.750 --> 06:39.520
I think baseball is better.

06:39.880 --> 06:42.820
What a wonderful topic!

06:42.820 --> 06:46.640
"Between baseball and soccer, 
I think baseball is better."

06:46.890 --> 06:49.340
If you agree baseball 
is better, vote "yes."

06:49.340 --> 06:51.880
If you think soccer is better, vote "no."

06:52.270 --> 06:54.160
Let the game begin!

06:56.430 --> 07:00.550
The Minority Rule game was on.

07:01.680 --> 07:05.400
We were forbidden from leaving the room 
while the game was in progress.

07:05.400 --> 07:08.400
Smartphones and other devices
 were confiscated, as well.

07:11.150 --> 07:16.030
Nao, I'm starting to get nervous.

07:16.970 --> 07:22.400
What if X has a plan to outsmart us?

07:22.400 --> 07:23.640
Oh, no!

07:23.640 --> 07:28.080
If we see Number 15 win 
this first round and survive,

07:28.080 --> 07:29.940
that's when we should really be afraid.

07:36.220 --> 07:39.880
I started keeping my eye
 on Number 15 exclusively.

07:40.380 --> 07:43.470
But he didn't do anything 
suspicious that I could see.

07:44.890 --> 07:50.060
As we'd discussed, members of our group 
began interacting with other players.

07:52.910 --> 07:56.840
But Akiyama-san stayed quiet 
and watched, as always.

07:58.680 --> 08:01.230
At any rate, the venue was 
as peaceful as could be.

08:02.160 --> 08:06.570
You would have hardly known we all 
had 100 million yen on the line.

08:07.730 --> 08:09.620
Three minutes remain.

08:09.930 --> 08:13.980
And when that announcement 
rang out, the voting began...

08:15.200 --> 08:17.070
in a perfectly orderly fashion.

08:23.390 --> 08:24.780
It is time.

08:28.360 --> 08:30.520
That started the tally.

08:35.790 --> 08:39.020
Our team had decided the day before

08:39.310 --> 08:43.040
to divide along these lines.

08:43.360 --> 08:45.110
And when I saw the result...

08:46.310 --> 08:49.550
Ten votes for "yes."
Twelve votes for "no."

08:49.550 --> 08:52.550
Accordingly, the yeses win.

08:52.550 --> 08:54.100
I won!

08:54.100 --> 08:57.810
I must now ask those who 
voted "no" to leave at once.

08:57.810 --> 09:00.390
"Yes" was the minority!

09:00.750 --> 09:02.590
I'm still in the game!

09:05.460 --> 09:07.720
Looks like we're gone now...

09:07.720 --> 09:09.520
We're counting on you.

09:11.290 --> 09:12.490
Nao.

09:12.490 --> 09:14.680
Take a good look at the board.

09:26.200 --> 09:27.580
Akiyama-san!

09:27.580 --> 09:31.060
This is terrible! Number 15 survived!

09:31.060 --> 09:32.290
I see.

09:32.290 --> 09:33.880
But more importantly...

09:34.230 --> 09:35.870
Something strange is going on here.

09:37.010 --> 09:38.780
This whole setup...

09:40.780 --> 09:42.210
Something's off.

09:43.070 --> 09:44.670
Off?

09:45.230 --> 09:47.120
You don't sense it?

09:47.660 --> 09:48.860
No.

09:48.860 --> 09:50.390
The game just now...

09:50.390 --> 09:53.370
It was the barest minimum split,
 ten to twelve.

09:54.070 --> 09:57.480
If the next round also splits 
into the minimum of four to six,

09:57.480 --> 10:01.140
it'd suggest we're acting 
under the worst-case scenario.

10:06.160 --> 10:10.300
The ten remaining players
 will proceed to the second round.

10:10.300 --> 10:11.750
Our questioner will be...

10:12.180 --> 10:16.660
What do we do? Change up the plan?

10:17.060 --> 10:19.120
No, we'll proceed as we are.

10:19.790 --> 10:22.800
Number 11, please come up to the stage.

10:23.070 --> 10:26.560
Watch everyone even more closely.

10:26.840 --> 10:27.680
Okay.

10:28.230 --> 10:30.890
Please pose your topic.

10:30.890 --> 10:33.060
Uh, well...

10:33.380 --> 10:37.310
Between S and M, I'm definitely an S.

10:37.310 --> 10:39.160
We have our topic.

10:39.160 --> 10:42.130
Those who consider 
themselves an S, vote "yes."

10:42.130 --> 10:44.700
Those who feel they are an M, vote "no."

10:46.450 --> 10:47.980
Come on, let's split up.

10:47.980 --> 10:49.450
Um, Akiyama-san...

10:50.160 --> 10:52.390
What do "S" and "M" mean?

10:52.720 --> 10:53.600
Huh?

10:53.950 --> 10:55.740
W-Well...

10:55.740 --> 10:59.180
I-It's like... playing offense or defense.

10:59.180 --> 11:02.490
S stands for sword, 
and M stands for moat.

11:03.830 --> 11:05.120
I see.

11:07.310 --> 11:10.290
Where there had been 22 players, 
there were now ten.

11:11.060 --> 11:15.730
Anyone acting suspiciously 
was bound to stand out.

11:16.100 --> 11:18.370
The food here is really something.

11:18.370 --> 11:20.690
I wonder how much it cost.

11:20.690 --> 11:22.860
Have you noticed anything, Hitomi-san?

11:22.860 --> 11:26.870
Akiyama-san said that
 this whole thing is... off.

11:26.870 --> 11:28.280
Off?

11:28.280 --> 11:31.230
You think he's up to something?

11:32.000 --> 11:34.980
He didn't say it was because of Number 15,

11:34.980 --> 11:38.090
but he made it sound like 
someone's plotting something.

11:39.130 --> 11:40.960
What could it be?

11:40.960 --> 11:46.160
All right. I'll use the next six hours
 to feel out the other players.

11:46.160 --> 11:49.730
Don't take your eyes
 off Number 15. All right?

11:49.730 --> 11:50.620
Right.

11:54.790 --> 11:57.670
I kept a close eye on Number 15.

11:58.990 --> 12:03.080
But I didn't see him do anything suspect.

12:03.590 --> 12:05.620
Time passed, and that was all.

12:06.540 --> 12:08.490
We only have an hour left.

12:08.490 --> 12:11.620
We need to decide who's voting yes and no.

12:11.620 --> 12:13.790
Which do you prefer, Hitomi-san?

12:13.790 --> 12:16.220
Let's see. I'll go for yes.

12:16.220 --> 12:17.870
I'm an S all the way!

12:17.870 --> 12:18.870
What about you?

12:18.870 --> 12:21.120
I'm fine either way.

12:21.120 --> 12:23.000
Vote yes, then!

12:23.000 --> 12:26.770
If I end up staying in, 
I'd love to have you with me.

12:26.770 --> 12:29.450
We girls are in this together.

12:29.450 --> 12:30.470
Well...

12:31.160 --> 12:34.770
Or are you with Akiyama to the end?

12:34.770 --> 12:37.130
You two together or something?

12:37.130 --> 12:39.030
Oh, no, certainly not!

12:39.030 --> 12:44.550
The truth was that I'd hoped to stay 
with Akiyama-san through it all.

12:45.250 --> 12:46.220
But...

12:46.780 --> 12:51.030
No, it's best if we split up this time.

12:51.810 --> 12:54.940
You and I were the ones 
who proposed the alliance.

12:54.940 --> 12:59.660
If we're always joined at the hip, 
people might get suspicious.

13:00.560 --> 13:04.110
We need to prioritize team unity for now.

13:07.750 --> 13:11.000
I've decided to split up 
with Akiyama-san this time.

13:11.000 --> 13:13.050
Great, then it's just us girls!

13:13.760 --> 13:17.390
But he says if we split up, 
we shouldn't have just women on one side.

13:18.560 --> 13:23.750
If something happens, it would be better 
to have a male-female pair stick around.

13:23.750 --> 13:27.070
So Akiyama-san thinks 
Matsubara-san and I should vote no,

13:28.090 --> 13:32.320
and the two of you should vote yes.

13:32.980 --> 13:34.650
I see.

13:35.580 --> 13:39.070
We finished the second-round voting

13:39.610 --> 13:41.280
and awaited the tally.

13:43.720 --> 13:46.090
I will now announce the votes.

13:46.970 --> 13:48.600
Number 12: "No."

13:49.550 --> 13:51.730
Number 3: "Yes."

13:51.730 --> 13:53.600
Number 1: "No."

13:53.600 --> 13:56.870
If the next round also splits 
into the minimum of four to six,

13:57.850 --> 14:00.240
it'd suggest we're acting
under the worst-case scenario.

14:00.810 --> 14:02.110
Don't tell me...

14:04.860 --> 14:06.970
We have our result!

14:07.360 --> 14:11.610
With a vote of four to six,
the yeses are in the minority.

14:12.100 --> 14:15.590
It's just as Akiyama-san predicted!

14:20.760 --> 14:25.260
The majority "no" voters 
must now leave the venue.

14:30.550 --> 14:33.940
Akiyama-san, Hitomi-san... Good luck!

14:35.490 --> 14:39.160
What I spied then 
sent a chill up my spine.

14:42.660 --> 14:45.900
Hey, X is still here, isn't he?

14:46.470 --> 14:47.360
Yes.

14:48.490 --> 14:50.610
That is all for today.

14:50.610 --> 14:54.520
Tomorrow, we will begin at eight 
and resume with these four players.

14:54.520 --> 14:57.740
Now, do enjoy your respite.

15:10.170 --> 15:13.450
Nao Kanzaki

15:14.060 --> 15:15.360
Hello?

15:15.800 --> 15:18.550
Oh, it's you. Where are you?

15:18.550 --> 15:22.250
At home. I just got in.

15:22.800 --> 15:25.370
Did the tournament office 
hound you for money?

15:25.370 --> 15:27.860
No. Not yet.

15:28.190 --> 15:32.440
Anyway, I guess things turned out 
the way you feared they would, huh?

15:32.440 --> 15:36.630
Yeah, X is definitely up to something.

15:36.630 --> 15:38.090
I knew it...

15:38.090 --> 15:39.830
Mind if I hang up now?

15:39.830 --> 15:44.590
If I don't get to work, we'll lose 
in tomorrow's game for sure.

15:44.590 --> 15:46.030
We'll lose?!

15:46.030 --> 15:47.390
So goodnight.

15:49.850 --> 15:52.740
What do I do? What do I do?!

15:56.550 --> 15:59.560
I couldn't stop fretting.

15:59.560 --> 16:04.050
So the next morning, I went to the 
building where the game was taking place.

16:05.930 --> 16:08.110
What? You're here?

16:08.110 --> 16:10.850
I was too nervous to stay home...

16:11.240 --> 16:15.080
That's no reason to come all 
the way back to the venue.

16:15.490 --> 16:18.170
But it's not just me.

16:18.170 --> 16:20.960
I ran into that Number 1 fellow.

16:21.420 --> 16:24.000
He seemed nervous, too...

16:24.920 --> 16:26.750
Mr. Number 22.

16:26.750 --> 16:29.220
The game will be starting soon.

16:29.220 --> 16:31.260
Please come to the meeting room.

16:31.530 --> 16:33.750
I'll call you back when it's over.

16:33.750 --> 16:34.780
Go home at once.

16:34.780 --> 16:35.660
Go home at once.

16:39.990 --> 16:42.010
Number 3, please come up to the stage.

16:42.010 --> 16:45.010
Me?! Oh, goodness...

16:46.570 --> 16:49.510
Let's see. What should I pick?

16:50.020 --> 16:51.940
Oh, I know.

16:51.940 --> 16:56.280
Out of the four of us, 
I'm the one who will win!

16:56.280 --> 16:59.490
We have another wonderful topic.

16:59.490 --> 17:03.880
"Out of the four of us, 
I'm the one who will win."

17:04.510 --> 17:07.310
Those who think they will win, vote "yes."

17:07.310 --> 17:09.780
Those who think they will lose, vote "no."

17:10.330 --> 17:12.090
Let the game begin!

17:19.050 --> 17:22.730
I'm so bored. 
There's nothing to do at this point.

17:22.730 --> 17:27.230
But that means X can't 
do anything either, right?

17:31.580 --> 17:33.480
What do you think you're doing?

17:34.320 --> 17:39.120
This will make it harder to open, 
so my vote should be tallied last.

17:39.120 --> 17:40.350
At least, that's the idea.

17:40.740 --> 17:43.750
What does the order matter? 
It won't change the result.

17:44.690 --> 17:46.030
True enough.

17:48.500 --> 17:51.760
Why, if it isn't Nao-chan! 
What are you doing here?

17:51.760 --> 17:53.750
Oh, the lawyer!

17:53.750 --> 17:56.220
You lost yesterday, didn't you?

17:56.220 --> 17:59.140
Shouldn't you be out there 
earning money to pay your debt?

17:59.140 --> 18:01.730
I-I haven't lost yet!

18:01.730 --> 18:04.000
We're going to win for sure!

18:04.000 --> 18:08.010
"We're going to win for sure"?

18:08.010 --> 18:12.730
Two of the remaining four 
are working with me.

18:12.730 --> 18:14.770
We have a surefire strategy!

18:15.050 --> 18:18.030
A surefire strategy, huh?

18:18.310 --> 18:22.030
And yet you still came
 because you're worried, right?

18:26.030 --> 18:28.750
The vote should be wrapping up soon.

18:28.750 --> 18:31.530
Well? You wanna come watch?

18:31.530 --> 18:33.340
What? Is that all right?

18:33.340 --> 18:34.790
Sure. Come on in.

18:35.620 --> 18:37.590
Thank you so much!

18:46.290 --> 18:47.810
Time is up.

18:50.920 --> 18:52.310
Akiyama-san!

18:53.560 --> 18:55.310
Nao! What are you doing here?

18:55.310 --> 18:57.720
What is the meaning of this?

18:57.720 --> 19:02.460
Um, one of the officials said I could 
watch if I stay behind the ropes.

19:02.460 --> 19:04.660
Yes, that is acceptable.

19:04.660 --> 19:07.120
The voting has just concluded.

19:07.120 --> 19:10.760
Now, let us tally the votes.

19:13.330 --> 19:16.460
It'll be all right, won't it, Akiyama-san?

19:16.460 --> 19:19.120
I've done everything I can, at least.

19:20.400 --> 19:22.460
First, Number 11...

19:24.800 --> 19:25.860
"No."

19:29.210 --> 19:30.980
Next, Number 3...

19:33.330 --> 19:34.440
"Yes."

19:35.580 --> 19:36.810
Number 15...

19:39.600 --> 19:41.740
This will decide it.

19:42.600 --> 19:46.620
Our team has one vote 
each for yes and no.

19:46.620 --> 19:50.300
If Number 15 votes yes, 
it'll be a two-to-two tie.

19:50.300 --> 19:53.230
But if he votes no, we win!

19:54.130 --> 19:58.640
Please, let it be no! Let it be no!

19:58.640 --> 20:00.970
Number 15: "No."

20:02.750 --> 20:05.510
We did it! We win!

20:05.510 --> 20:08.500
Akiyama-san! We win, don't we?!

20:08.500 --> 20:14.150
All thanks to your flawless plan! 
X didn't stand a chance!

20:14.150 --> 20:16.390
Come on, would you chill out already?

20:16.390 --> 20:18.450
Hitomi-san, we did it!

20:18.450 --> 20:20.020
We won, didn't we?!

20:20.020 --> 20:21.610
I'm so happy!

20:24.100 --> 20:25.530
Hitomi-san?

20:25.530 --> 20:29.170
Nao, you really are stupid.

20:29.690 --> 20:32.010
"We" didn't win.

20:32.010 --> 20:33.410
I won.

20:33.760 --> 20:36.660
Huh? What are you
 talking about, Hitomi-san?

20:36.660 --> 20:40.190
And for your information, 
my name isn't Hitomi.

20:40.190 --> 20:43.010
My real name is Yuji Fukunaga.

20:43.420 --> 20:46.670
Hitomi Miyahara is my roommate.

20:46.670 --> 20:52.990
I borrowed her invite to the Liar Game.

20:46.680 --> 20:51.430
Ms. Hitomi Miyahara

20:46.680 --> 20:51.430
Welcome to Round 2

20:52.990 --> 20:57.810
Yuji Fukunaga? But that 
sounds like a man's name...

20:57.810 --> 21:00.680
That's right. The truth is...

21:01.470 --> 21:03.430
I am a man!

21:04.940 --> 21:07.760
Just someone you could 
call female-presenting.

21:08.370 --> 21:10.370
You had no idea?

21:10.370 --> 21:12.730
I don't know what you're...

21:12.730 --> 21:14.450
And that's not all.

21:14.450 --> 21:18.040
I'm actually X.

21:18.040 --> 21:19.070
What?!

21:19.070 --> 21:24.290
In other words, the "young man" 
who stole this from Michiko Takada...

21:24.630 --> 21:27.040
was none other than me.

21:27.920 --> 21:30.330
You really don't have 
a brain in your head!

21:30.330 --> 21:33.060
You seriously let X onto your own team!

21:33.060 --> 21:38.060
And in addition to being "X," I'm not 
Hitomi Miyahara, but Yuji Fukunaga.

21:38.580 --> 21:41.040
Do you realize what that means?

21:41.040 --> 21:45.440
I used "Hitomi Miyahara" on that contract.

21:45.440 --> 21:48.470
But that isn't my real name.

21:45.440 --> 21:52.950
Hitomi Miyahara

21:48.470 --> 21:52.950
It's not the signature of the 
real Hitomi Miyahara, either.

21:52.950 --> 21:58.360
In other words, you can't enforce 
that ridiculous contract on me!

21:58.360 --> 22:01.850
That 2.1 billion is all mine!

22:01.850 --> 22:04.950
And you absolute fools fell for my trap!

22:09.960 --> 22:13.280
No... That can't be...

23:45.020 --> 23:50.060
Next Time

23:45.020 --> 23:50.060
Initiative
